Hello all,

I've tried to compile Nethack 3.4.3 on a Linux/Debian system.

After running sh /sys/unix/setup.sh I've made the appropriate changes in
include/config.h, src/Makefile and the top level Makefile.

Compiling only with tty support works fine, but compiling with tty and
X11 support fails.

In the top Makefile I've enabled
,----
| VARDATND x11tiles NetHack.ad pet_mark.xbm rip.xpm
|.
|.
|.
| WINSRC = $(WINTTYSRC) $(WINX11SRC)
| WINOBJ = $(WINTTYOBJ) $(WINX11OBJ)
| .
| .
| .
| WINLIB = $(WINTTYLIB) $(WINX11LIB)
`----

and in include/config.h

,----
| #define TTY_GRAPHICS	/* good old tty based graphics */
| #define X11_GRAPHICS	/* X11 interface */
| .
| .
| .
| 
| # define USE_XPM		/* Disable if you do not have the XPM library */
| # ifdef USE_XPM
| #  define GRAPHIC_TOMBSTONE	/* Use graphical tombstone (rip.xpm) */
| # endif
| #endif
`----

I've also set in src/Makefile

,----
| # libraries for X11
| # If USE_XPM is defined in config.h, you will also need -lXpm here.
| WINX11LIB = -lXaw -lXmu -lXpm -lXext -lXt -lX11
`----

Unfortunately all this results in

../win/X11/dialogs.c:51: X11/Xaw/Cardinals.h: No such file or directory
../win/X11/dialogs.c:52: X11/Xaw/Form.h: No such file or directory
../win/X11/dialogs.c:53: X11/Xaw/Label.h: No such file or directory
../win/X11/dialogs.c:54: X11/Xaw/AsciiText.h: No such file or directory
../win/X11/dialogs.c:54: X11/Xaw/Command.h: No such file or directory
make[1]: *** [dialogs.o] Error 1
Make : *** [nethack] Error 2

Any ideas how to make the compiling?

